  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `assets/posts/fanuc.cps`: the section preamble is now `G90 G17 G94 <wcs> G40 G49 G80`. Before, it was `G90 <wcs> G40 G49 G80`. The post also sets its plane memory (`planeG`) to 17 after the block.\n- `assets/posts/doosan-dnm.cps`: the section preamble is now `G90 G17 G94 <wcs> G40 G49 G80`. Before, it had no `G94`.\n- 77 recorded programs are made again. Each one changes only in its preamble line.\n- `docs/decisions/4346-preamble-g17-g94.md` records the decision.\n\n## Cause\n\nA FANUC control can keep G18 / G19 or G95 from an earlier program, from MDI or from its power-on parameters (FANUC Series 0i-F operator's manual B-64604EN-2). The Fanuc preamble did not state the plane or the feed mode. The Doosan DNM preamble did not state the feed mode. Then XY arcs, cutter compensation and drilling cycles can run in the wrong plane. An F word in mm/min is then read as mm per revolution. Neither post writes G93 or G95, so G94 is always the correct mode.\n\n## Tests\n\n- New pin: `fanuc_post::preamble::the_fanuc_family_preamble_states_g17_and_g94_before_the_first_motion` (`crates/post/tests/fanuc_post/preamble.rs`). It is a module of the existing `fanuc_post` binary, not a new top-level test. It posts two sections through each of the two posts. It checks that each preamble has `G17` and `G94` and that the first preamble comes before the first motion.\n- Red before the fix: \"fanuc: the preamble `G90 G54 G40 G49 G80` states G17\".\n- Mutation checks, one post at a time:\n  - old `fanuc.cps` with the new `doosan-dnm.cps`: red;\n  - old `doosan-dnm.cps` with the new `fanuc.cps`: red (\"doosan-dnm: the preamble `G90 G17 G54 G40 G49 G80` states G94\");\n  - both new: green.\n- `conformance::the_dialects_actually_differ`: with the fix, Fanuc and Doosan DNM write the same `drill_peck` program. Before, the missing G17 was their only difference there, and that was the defect. Each Doosan DNM word (brake, conveyor, AICC) is opt-in. Now a pair that is identical on `drill_peck` must differ on a rotary index on the DNM machine file with `rotaryBrake: true`. The test still finds two scripts that are copies of each other.\n- Literal asserts that read `G90 G54` / `G90 G55` as the work-offset word now read `G94 G54` / `G94 G55`. Their purpose does not change. Files: `crates/app/tests/posting.rs`, `crates/app/tests/setup_mount_trace.rs` and `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests.rs`. The full-preamble literals changed in `crates/app/tests/mcp_open/mod.rs`, `crates/post/tests/doosan_dnm_post.rs` and `crates/post/tests/declared_options.rs`.\n\nCommands and results on the final head `129ebbe6e`, base `9fb406cd6`:\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base 9fb406cd6...`: 867 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled. This includes `app suites: example_catalog`, `example_catalog_adaptive` and `example_catalog_edge_work`.\n- `cargo xtask gate light --base 9fb406cd6...`: 6 steps, 0 failed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean. The same for `-p camcraft-app` and `-p camcraft-ui`.\n- No heavy step: this is a P3, and AGENTS.md \"Heavy lanes at review\" gives a heavy step only to a P1 under the safety floor.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\n77 programs. Every changed line is the preamble line and nothing else (`git diff -U0`, counted):\n\n- 73 `G90 G54 G40 G49 G80` and 23 `G90 G17 G54 G40 G49 G80` became `G90 G17 G94 G54 G40 G49 G80`;\n- 1 `G90 G55 ...` and 1 `G90 G17 G55 ...` became `G90 G17 G94 G55 G40 G49 G80`;\n- 2 Explain goldens: the comment on the preamble now reads `(ABSOLUTE POSITIONS, XY PLANE, FEED PER MINUTE)`. The comment cap (60 characters) drops the work-offset words, as it did before for the words that did not fit.\n\nGroups:\n\n- `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/` (Fanuc, Doosan DNM, inch, explain, inverted, wcs-flip, probe and synth programs), written by `WRITE_GOLDEN=1` on `conformance`, `fanuc_post` and the app suites;\n- `crates/post/tests/recorded/golden/fanuc/` and `.../doosan-dnm/`, written by `WRITE_GOLDEN=1` on `script_fanuc` and `script_doosan_dnm`;\n- `examples/catalog/*/*/*.nc` (9 programs), written by `cargo xtask catalog`. The tool also rewrote the `.camproj` files (project version 83 to 84). I put those back, because that change is not part of this fix;\n- `examples/first-part.nc`, written by `camcraft-cli process`;\n- `docs/tester-kits/fanuc-mgi-blank/mgi_blank_{box,bar}.nc`. This kit has no writer, so I changed the one preamble line in each file. `fanuc_mgi_blank::the_tester_kit_is_what_the_post_writes` passes on it.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No run on a real control.\n- The full heavy lanes. They run at the cut.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nNone. When I claimed the issue, no open PR touched `fanuc.cps` or `doosan-dnm.cps`. #4347 and #4348 merged after my first base. This branch is made again on `9fb406cd6`, which contains both.\n\nEffort: high (no escalation).\n\nChangelog: The Fanuc mill post now writes G17 and G94 in each section preamble, and the Doosan DNM post writes G94, so a control left in G18 / G19 or G95 runs the program in the XY plane and in mm/min.\n\nFixes #4346\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
